<title>BELGIUM: BOE's George hopes for deal on lira.</title>
<headline>BOE's George hopes for deal on lira.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said on Sunday he believed there was a consensus among EU countries on a central parity rate for the Italian lira in the exchange rate mechanism.</p>
<p>&quot;I should think so,&quot; he told reporters when asked about a deal as he entered a meeting of EU finance ministers and central bank governors.  </p>
<p>The meeting was taking place following the failure of the EU's monetary committee on Saturday to agree a rate for the lira to rejoin the ERM.</p>
<p>Italy asked for a rate of 1,010 lira to the German mark. Its partners want a rate of less than 1,000, officials said.</p>
</text>
